 "poem": "XIII. OMNES DE ILLUMINUS domine.\n145    Now come, and now go; for th' hour,\nThat thou hast all the hours of heaven,\nIs come again: thou liv'st long still again,\nAnd yet uncomplac'd art thou alive.\nAll is too long thy clock to hour;\nThe whole are too short at last to hour;\nBut time has done in him who gave given\nHis soul unto us for ours again:\nThere are too many years before us,\nToo late a spring for us to reap before,\nA summer when we have need more enough,",
